```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    %% Sequence diagram: from device hardware to backend processing and events
    participant Browser as UserDevice\n(Browser)
    participant Signaling as SignalingServer\n(FastAPI+WebSocket)
    participant MediaServer as MediaServer\n(aiortc or SFU)
    participant MediaProcessor as MediaProcessor\n(ASR/CV/VAD)
    participant ASR as ASR_Service\n(Model/Whisper/Vosk)
    participant EventBus as EventBus\n(WebSocket/Event Delivery)
    participant Frontend as Frontend\n(Widgets)

    Browser->>Browser: getUserMedia()
    Browser->>Browser: create RTCPeerConnection, addTrack(Audio/Video)
    Browser->>Signaling: send {type: "webrtc-offer", sdp}
    Signaling->>MediaServer: forward offer (controller or direct)
    MediaServer-->>Signaling: answer SDP
    Signaling-->>Browser: send answer
    Browser->>Browser: setRemoteDescription(answer)
    Browser-->>Signaling: exchange ICE candidates (via WebSocket)
    Note over Browser,MediaServer: DTLS / SRTP handshake — secure media channel
    Browser-->>MediaServer: RTP media packets (Opus for audio, VP8/VP9 for video)
    MediaServer-->>MediaProcessor: deliver decoded frames / PCM
    MediaProcessor->>ASR: resample -> submit audio frames
    ASR-->>MediaProcessor: partial/final transcript
    MediaProcessor->>EventBus: publish TranscriptionEvent / DetectionEvent
    EventBus->>Frontend: push event to widgets (transcript, commands)
    Frontend->>Browser: update UI / show results

    %% Optional: Video CV path
    MediaProcessor->>MediaProcessor: run CV pipeline (MediaPipe / OpenCV)
    MediaProcessor->>EventBus: publish GestureDetected

```
